# The shipped path (the release carries no r8 sidecar): the own Q3_K_M (bq3km) against the 1017 Q3_K_M with
# BLOOMERY_R8=off, prompt and decode at P = 512 and 4096. Earlier sittings: with r8 on, the default file was 7 % / 23 %
# faster in pp at 512 / 4096 (bq3km-speed) and the r8off card put the gap on the sidecar's row-lane tile; its two-round
# arms (cold rows inside) read pp @4096 330 (default, r8 off) against 364 (bq3km), too wide to decide on.
# Decomposition [derived]: with r8 off both files run the one-row Q3_K tile over the same routed types (gate/up Q3_K,
# down Q4_K/Q5_K) and the same host slots within 1 %; the residual differences are the router (F32 here, BF16 there),
# the engram layout and the residency plan, each worth under 2 % of a layer-batch. Expected: equal within the ruler.
kind: profile
question: on the path the release ships (no sidecar), does the own Q3_K_M prompt and decode at the default file's speed?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096 prose, bq3km, --place a, RTX A6000, beside the default file at BLOOMERY_R8=off in the same
  invocation (P = 512 and decode rows alongside)
unit: tok/s
predict: 330..400
condition: one lease, main's generate_ds41, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3 just depth-gpu-ds41 prose:512@BLOOMERY_R8=off
  prose:4096@BLOOMERY_R8=off prose:512@BLOOMERY_V41_MODEL=/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km-00001-of-00009.gguf,BLOOMERY_REF_MODEL=/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km-00001-of-00009.gguf
  prose:4096@BLOOMERY_V41_MODEL=/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km-00001-of-00009.gguf,BLOOMERY_REF_MODEL=/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-bq3km-00001-of-00009.gguf, order rotated every round; the load lines read r8=off in
  all arms; no row [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]; cold rows left out of the judgement
decide-in: pp and decode within 3 % of the default's r8-off rows at both P (or faster): the shipped-path speed holds;
  the default flip is the user's call with the loss table
decide-below: slower by more than 3 %: read stat prefill per arm; the router/engram/residency term is the suspect
decide-above: faster: same lines; the flip carries a speed gain on the shipped path
# Outcome (2026-11-15, A6000 300 W, place a, main e2149c1ed's generate_ds41, 3 rounds, order rotated, every load line
#  r8=off, no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row): pp @ 4096 bq3km 403.10 (395.42..411.81, cold 0/3) against the default's
#  387.73 (372.71..409.94, cold 1/3), +4.0 %; pp @ 512 237.99 (219.19..254.59, cold 1/3) against 245.21 (244.47..246.02),
#  -2.9 %, its spread 16 % from the cold row; decode @ 512 45.34 against 45.72 (-0.8 %), @ 4096 37.04 against 37.06.
#  decide-in: on the shipped path the own file holds the default's speed (faster at 4096, inside 3 % at 512); the flip
#  is the user's call with the loss table, after the file is rewritten with the full down importance (imxdown).
